{"action": "answer", "found": true, "answer": "Only one agreement in the material I read states a minimum fee as a specific dollar amount: the VerticalNet Maintenance and Support Agreement (VerticalNet/VNE and Converge, 2001-10-09). It sets an Initial Term Minimum Fee of $4,500,000, payable in 18 equal monthly installments of $250,000. Minimum fees for any renewal term are not fixed; they are to be mutually determined by the parties.

The BNL Outsourcing Agreement (VIP and BNL) refers to a defined "Minimum Fee" in its termination provision, which sets a cancellation fee equal to the greatest of three amounts: (i) the Minimum Fee times the remaining months, (ii) the average monthly billings over the prior six months times the remaining months, or (iii) $30,000. The $30,000 is a floor on the cancellation fee, not a stated minimum fee. In the text I read, I did not find the dollar amount of the Minimum Fee itself.

I did not find a stated dollar minimum fee commitment for Corio, Seaspine or Dynamex, and I did not locate any amendments. I did not search those documents thoroughly, so the answer for them is not confirmed either way.", "citations": ["verticalnet", "bnl"]}
